From d00be293b9bb16e44233d643b5e08848e7778013 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HaeImAlan <me@haeimalan.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 10:53:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Fog of war

Players are only tracked for viewers that could see them (anti-ESP), after VALORANT's fog of war. Both sides are swept over a lookahead of the viewer's ping plus two check intervals, along their momentum, and the viewer may look from a third person camera up to fogOfWar.camera-distance away (clipped at walls), so players are revealed before they can come into sight. Sounds, block effects and particles caused by a hidden player are not sent either. The rays run on fogOfWar.threads workers over a main thread snapshot; the main thread applies each result one check later. fogOfWar.log-interval-seconds logs per world statistics. Off by default: fogOfWar.enabled in cubing.yml.

